+### Non-Bronze S3 retention cleanup
+
+`cleanup-s3-storage.sh` enforces the fixed 24-hour retention boundary without
+ever accepting the Bronze bucket as a target. It preserves every latest object
+and latest delete marker under `warehouse/silver/`; historical Silver versions
+and all non-Silver Warehouse objects become eligible after 24 hours. The
+removed Snowflake-export bucket is not a cleanup target.
+
+Always generate and review a dry-run plan first:
+
+```bash
+bash infra/scripts/cleanup-s3-storage.sh \
+  --env prod \
+  --aws-profile sec_platform_deployer \
+  --aws-account-id 690839588395 \
+  --output-file /tmp/prod-s3-retention-plan.json
+```
+
+Applying is a separate destructive operator action. It requires both an audit
+file and an exact acknowledgement of the fixed retention period:
+
+```bash
+bash infra/scripts/cleanup-s3-storage.sh \
+  --env prod \
+  --aws-profile sec_platform_deployer \
+  --aws-account-id 690839588395 \
+  --output-file /tmp/prod-s3-retention-applied.json \
+  --confirm-retention-hours 24 \
+  --apply
+```
+
+The script verifies the authenticated AWS account through STS, rejects Bronze,
+rejects cross-environment/account and role-swapped bucket names, addresses exact
+S3 version IDs in batches, and leaves the pre-mutation plan on disk if an apply
+fails partway. Do not schedule it until at least one production dry run has been
+reviewed and the post-cleanup Silver acceptance checks are defined.
